# Parallel Subagents

Spawn subagents when independent workstreams can be investigated without sharing mutable
state: separate files, separate hypotheses, separate test failures, or separate review
perspectives.

Use one subagent per independent workstream. The default is read-only. Do not allow
recursive fan-out unless the user explicitly requests it. Wait for all results before
synthesis unless the user asks for streaming status.

Synthesize findings by evidence quality. Preserve conflicts and resolve them through
deterministic tests, source inspection, official documentation, or reproduction.

Serialize edits unless files are disjoint and the write plan is explicit. Validate after
merging findings or changes.
